-- fires against the real artifact.


-- The class itself. INSERT ... WHERE NOT EXISTS rather than INSERT OR IGNORE,
-- so re-running the script is a no-op instead of a silent partial write.
INSERT INTO imported_classes (class_id, name, system, markdown, status, created_by)
SELECT 'space-wolfen', 'Space Wolfen', 'rifts', '---
id: space-wolfen
name: Space Wolfen
system: rifts
category: rcc
source_book: Rifts Dimension Book 2: Phase World p.65-66
attribute_dice:
  IQ: "3d6"
  ME: "3d6"
  MA: "2d6"
  PS: "4d6+1"
  PP: "3d6"
  PE: "3d6"
  PB: "3d6"
  Spd: "4d6"
ppe_base: "3d6"
bonuses:
  pools: { sdc: 30 }
  combat: { initiative: 2, attacks: 1 }
natural_abilities:
  - { name: "Nightvision", description: "40 feet (12.2 m), with keen colour vision." }
  - { name: "Superior Smell and Hearing", description: "Recognize a common or known smell 50% +3% per level of experience. Track by smell alone 20% +4% per level of experience." }
  - { name: "Bite", description: "2D4 S.D.C." }
  - { name: "Claws", description: "1D6 S.D.C. plus P.S. damage bonus." }
  - { name: "Two Attacks Untrained", description: "A wolfen gets two hand to hand attacks with no combat training at all, or one plus whatever hand to hand and boxing give." }
  - { name: "Horror Factor", description: "12. A number the wolfen projects, which the sheet has no field for." }
  - { name: "Average Life Span", description: "120+ years. Ultra-tech health care has more than doubled the wolfen''s natural span." }
  - { name: "Size", description: "Seven to nine feet tall (2.1 to 2.7 m), 350 to 500 pounds (157.5 to 225 kg)." }
extraction_notes: |
  - Read from the OCR cache of a scan and verified against a 200 dpi render of
    printed 66, which carries everything from Horror Factor down. The attributes
    and the S.D.C. line are on printed 65 and both pages were read to the end.
  - THE 30 S.D.C. IS A POOL BONUS, NOT sdc_base. The book says "30 S.D.C. plus
    those gained from O.C.C.s and physical skills", so it stacks on top of the
    occupation''s roll. Written as sdc_base it would be SILENTLY wrong:
    combineClasses gives the race''s pool precedence over the occupation''s, and
    the character would carry 30 instead of 30 plus the O.C.C.''s dice. This is
    the same reading the catalog''s Palladium `wolfen` already gets for its 20.
  - "M.D.C.: By armor or magic only" - an S.D.C. being, so no mdc_base. No
    S.D.C. formula of its own either, so the core rule reaches it at 1D6 through
    CORE_SDC_BY_CLASS, and the 30 lands on top.
  - SAME SPECIES AS THE CATALOG''S `wolfen`, DIFFERENT ROW. Printed 52 says the
    wolfen of the Three Galaxies are identical to the denizens of the Palladium
    world, and the two stat blocks are close but not equal - this one has
    +2 initiative and an extra attack the Palladium entry does not, 30 S.D.C.
    against 20, and a 120-year life span against the Palladium book''s. It is its
    own R.C.C. in its own setting, so it is its own row rather than a variant.
  - Psionics are "Standard; basically same as humans", so there is no psionics
    block: the character rolls on the Random Psionics Table like anyone else.
  - A RACE CARRIES NO xp_table. The book gives the space wolfen no ladder;
    printed 183 heads the relevant column "Phase Adept, Time Master & Wolfen
    Quatoria", which is the O.C.C.''s.
  - THE MAGIC RESTRICTION IS PROSE, not a restriction block. The wolfen
    abandoned magic long ago and only those native to the Warlock Federation are
    likely to take a magic O.C.C. `occ_restrictions` matches an `occ_group`, and
    "unlikely unless from a particular federation" is not a group - it is a
    table rule, so it is in the GM Notes.
---

## Lore

The wolfen are large canine humanoids, and for all the animal in their
appearance they are among the most intelligent, cunning and resourceful species
in the Three Galaxies. Like humans they are found nearly everywhere, and are
admired and respected about as often as they are hated, envied and feared. The
civilization runs on honor, valor and strength, individually and as a whole.

Their organization and politics read like the ancient Roman Empire of Earth, and
their language and much of their terminology resemble Latin. Dimensional
travellers who notice cannot say whether that is parallel evolution or
transdimensional pollination - perhaps Romans visited the wolfen homeworld
millennia ago, or the traffic ran the other way.

## Two empires, one race

Not long ago the Wolfen Empire meant to unify a galaxy. The Consortium and the
Transgalactic Empire between them ended that. In the CCW the wolfen are one of
the leading partners of a galaxy-spanning confederation; in the Empire they are
an important client race, subordinate to the kreeghor.

Factions have taken that differently. Many have come to think the CCW a stronger
and longer-lasting thing than any wolfen-dominated nation ever was. Another
faction still believes in wolfen supremacy, running from ordinary pride in
wolfen work to outright xenophobia, and a few plot for the day their race takes
its rightful place. Those sentiments run through wolfen on both sides, which
makes for convoluted intrigue: Imperial supremacists may funnel aid to the
Freedom Fighters purely to advance their own cause, and will betray the rebels
the moment it profits them in the Empire.

Most wolfen have simply adapted, and are model CCW citizens. They are strongly
present in the Consortium Armed Forces at every level and have produced a great
many scientists, engineers and diplomats.

## GM Notes

CCW wolfen and Transgalactic wolfen hate each other with a passion, each side
holding the other traitors to the race. Even Freedom Fighters have to live with
it: CCW wolfen treat rebels against the Empire as *lost pups returning to the
fold*, which the rebels resent and accept anyway, because they need the help.

They work closely with humans and the seljuk and admire both - they think humans
pay too little attention to honor and have learned to forgive the immaturity.
Most dislike and distrust the noro while accepting them as equals.

The wolfen abandoned magic long ago; only one native to the Warlock Federation
is likely to take a magic O.C.C. Otherwise virtually any unrestricted O.C.C. is
open, and they lean to wilderness work, highly skilled warrior trades and
science. Many famous cosmo-knights were and are wolfen: the code of honor fits
the goals of the Cosmic Forge.

Most favour ancient weapon styles and the matching W.P.s. Millennia into
spaceflight, wolfen officials still carry ceremonial swords as a badge of office
- and a good many of those are not-so-ceremonial vibro-blades and phase swords.
', 'published', 'data-script'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'space-wolfen');


-- Read the result back rather than trusting the exit code. d1-apply prints
-- these, and a CR in the stored markdown means the checkout mangled the file.
SELECT class_id, name, status, length(markdown) AS bytes, instr(markdown, char(13)) > 0 AS has_cr
  FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'space-wolfen';

